# Copy to .env (gitignored) or export in your shell. This file IS the shipped
# default: fully local, no account, no key, nothing to pay. Every value is
# optional; OPENROUTER_API_KEY becomes required only if you move the answering
# model or the embeddings to OpenRouter (see the commented block below).

# LanceDB with cards_<backend> / transcripts_<backend> tables. Commented out: unset,
# the index is $AYL_HOME/index (~/AskYourLibrary/index), where
# scripts/ingest_demo_corpus.py builds the demo corpus. An index built before that
# default moved, in the checkout's data/lancedb, is read where it is until 0.5.0
# (docs/upgrading.md has the move). Set, the path is used exactly as written: no
# `~` is expanded, and a relative one is resolved against the working directory.
# LIBRARY_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/an/index

# Embeddings: ollama (local bge-m3, default) | openrouter
EMBED_BACKEND=ollama
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# Ollama 0.33 or newer for LLM_BACKEND=ollama: older builds ignore the reasoning_effort
# the client sends, and a thinking model then reasons without a bound (measured on 0.33.3).
OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=bge-m3

# Orchestrator LLM: local by default. LLM_BACKEND=ollama runs every agent node on a
# model Ollama serves — no account, no key, no cost, and the cost lines read $0.0000.
# OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL must be pulled (`ollama pull qwen2.5:14b`, 9.0 GB); `bash
# scripts/install-mac.sh` does that for you. In this mode the answering model is
# configured by the OLLAMA_* variables ONLY: ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL and PRICE_* are
# OpenRouter settings and are not applied, so nothing goes to OpenRouter by accident.
# Any value other than ollama|openrouter refuses to start rather than falling back.
LLM_BACKEND=ollama
OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b
#
# Hosted alternative — optional, and it costs money. LLM_BACKEND=openrouter sends the
# question and the retrieved passages to OpenRouter, which needs an account and a key
# (roughly $0.001 per research question on the demo core set at the rates below, and
# $0.0002 on the catalogue set; docs/cost.md has the arithmetic). The reports behind the
# README's results table were produced in this configuration on claude-sonnet-4.6, the
# hosted default before 2026-09-18, not in the local one; docs/eval-results/ also holds
# local runs, each naming its backend and model in its own header.
# To switch: set LLM_BACKEND=openrouter above,
# uncomment the three lines here, and put your key in OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731
# PRICE_IN_PER_MTOK=0.06
# PRICE_OUT_PER_MTOK=0.12
# The model above runs with its thinking off (LLM_REASONING=off, the default); with
# thinking on it was about three times slower (2.8x on the core set). `provider` leaves the model's own default.
# LLM_REASONING=off
# Backup, measured on the same questions (docs/eval-results/2026-09-18-hosted-models.md):
# replace the three lines above with these four (drop the "## "), about $0.02 per question.
# It was measured with its provider's default thinking, hence LLM_REASONING=provider.
## ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL=google/gemini-3.8-flash
## PRICE_IN_PER_MTOK=0.75
## PRICE_OUT_PER_MTOK=3.75
## LLM_REASONING=provider
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Also serves EMBED_BACKEND=openrouter, independently of where the answering model runs.
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# Output cap per LLM call (nodes return short JSON / short answers)
MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=2048
# What observe sees of each retrieved passage (ADR-025): search hit / chapter read.
# A transcript chunk is packed to 2,400 characters, so a search hit arrives whole and
# SEARCH_HIT_CHARS no longer cuts one — the chunk and the window are one decision.
SEARCH_HIT_CHARS=2500
CHAPTER_HIT_CHARS=12000
# How much of a chapter the chapter-read window may be chosen from, when the request
# says what it is looking for. A scan budget: the model still sees CHAPTER_HIT_CHARS.
CHAPTER_SCAN_CHARS=120000
# Loop budgets: steps per question, dry steps before the CRAG gate stops, steps in a row that may
# lose every quote to the provenance gate before such a step counts as dry, books a clarify
# offers (1-5).
# The measured numbers are for the defaults; the eval fingerprint names steps, window and backend.
MAX_STEPS=4
MAX_EMPTY_STREAK=2
MAX_DROPPED_STREAK=2
MAX_CLARIFY_CANDIDATES=5
# Time budgets: per-attempt timeout of one model call, extra attempts on a timeout or transient
# error, and the per-question deadline the loop checks before each next decision (0 = none; the
# clarify pause is not counted). Both values here are the LOCAL ones — a local model is slower and
# may load cold. config.py's own per-backend default for LLM_TIMEOUT_S is 600 under
# LLM_BACKEND=ollama and 120 otherwise, but a value in a copied .env is an environment value and
# wins over it, so the local number is written out rather than left to be inherited. The deadline
# is per backend for the same reason and by the same rule: 300 s is a hosted model's whole wall
# clock for four steps, which a cold local model can spend in the first one, so local gets twenty
# minutes. Both lines below are config.py's local defaults, written out, not a change to them.
# On the hosted backend, use LLM_TIMEOUT_S=120 and QUESTION_DEADLINE_S=300.
LLM_TIMEOUT_S=600
LLM_MAX_RETRIES=2
QUESTION_DEADLINE_S=1200
# Opt-in fallback: file scanned for OPENROUTER_API_KEY=... (unset = disabled)
OPENROUTER_ENV_FILE=
# Embedding model when EMBED_BACKEND=openrouter
OPENROUTER_EMBED_MODEL=openai/text-embedding-3-small

# UI language: en (default) | ua
ASK_LANG=en

# Where the agent writes raw-hit scratchpads (a human-readable log; validate does not
# read them). Unset, the CLI and `ayl ui` both write to $AYL_HOME/scratch. A `~` is
# expanded; a relative path would be resolved against whatever directory the command
# was run in, so set an absolute one.
# ASK_SCRATCH_DIR=~/AskYourLibrary/scratch

# Eval harness: golden set and where reports go
GOLDEN_PATH=eval/golden/en-demo.yaml
EVAL_RESULTS_DIR=eval/results

# Evidence must name the hit it was copied from; 0 resolves a missing hit id by
# the quote instead of dropping the item (still evidence-based)
AYL_STRICT_HIT_ID=1

# Optional LangSmith tracing (sends prompts and retrieved text to LangSmith).
# EU accounts also need: LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT=https://eu.api.smith.langchain.com
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=
LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=ask-your-library
# build_graph sets LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true whenever LANGCHAIN_API_KEY is set; the
# SDK also reads LANGSMITH_API_KEY + LANGSMITH_TRACING[_V2], which another
# project's shell may have exported. To keep tracing off whatever the
# environment inherited, set BOTH (LANGSMITH_TRACING_V2 is read first):
# LANGSMITH_TRACING_V2=false
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=false

# Chainlit web UI login; the auth secret is generated into AYL_CHAINLIT_DIR/auth-secret
# unless provided here. The login form's first field is labelled "Email address";
# type the username there.
CHAINLIT_USERNAME=admin
CHAINLIT_PASSWORD=change-me
# Leave unset to have the UI generate and persist one in AYL_CHAINLIT_DIR/auth-secret
# CHAINLIT_AUTH_SECRET=
# The UI refuses to start with the default password; exactly 1 allows it for a
# throwaway local demo (anything else is treated as "no")
# AYL_ALLOW_DEFAULT_LOGIN=1
# Where the UI keeps its chat db and auth secret (tests and the injection canary
# point this at a temp dir so the reader's own history is left alone). Unset, it is
# $AYL_HOME/ui/.chainlit — or, until 0.5.0, a checkout's .chainlit/ that already holds
# a chat.db. `ayl ui` also takes the Chainlit app root from the directory above it —
# where it writes the configuration it serves under — and uses AYL_HOME/ui when this
# is unset. An absolute path: a relative one is resolved against whatever directory
# the server was started in.
# AYL_CHAINLIT_DIR=~/AskYourLibrary/ui/.chainlit
# The reader's own folder, the home of everything built on this machine: the index
# ($AYL_HOME/index), the scratchpads, the web chat's state ($AYL_HOME/ui), the
# engineer's shelf's local cards, and later the private shelf. Outside any checkout:
# the default index and the local cards are refused inside a git work tree (set
# LIBRARY_DB_PATH to keep an index somewhere else).
# AYL_HOME=~/AskYourLibrary
# The UI also refuses to start without an OpenRouter key when one is needed (hosted answering
# model or hosted embeddings), so a missing key is reported before anyone logs in; 1 allows
# importing the UI module without one (tests)
# AYL_ALLOW_START_WITHOUT_KEY=1
# The login cookie is SameSite=strict, which the UI sets on Chainlit's cookie module itself.
# CHAINLIT_COOKIE_SAMESITE is deliberately not listed here: `chainlit run` has already read it
# before the UI is loaded, so neither this file nor an exported value decides the policy.
